From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:49:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] PCI: cadence: hpa: never program a zero root port ID

cdns_pcie_hpa_host_setup() writes the root port vendor and device ID
whenever the value differs from 0xffff. The IDs are read from the
"vendor-id"/"device-id" properties only if the caller left them 0 or
0xffff; when neither the caller nor the firmware provides them, a
zero-initialised cdns_pcie_rc keeps 0 and the root port is reprogrammed
to 0000:0000.

Treat a still-zero ID after the property lookup as "not provided" and
keep the value the controller reports.
---
 drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pcie-cadence-host-hpa.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pcie-cadence-host-hpa.c b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pcie-cadence-host-hpa.c
index fcd1361e0a71..2b40ece71364 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pcie-cadence-host-hpa.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/cadence/pcie-cadence-host-hpa.c
@@ -477,6 +477,15 @@ int cdns_pcie_hpa_host_setup(struct cdns_pcie_rc *rc)
 		device_property_read_u32(dev, "vendor-id", &rc->vendor_id);
 	if (rc->device_id == 0 || rc->device_id == 0xffff)
 		device_property_read_u32(dev, "device-id", &rc->device_id);
+	/*
+	 * Nothing provided an ID: keep the value the controller reports. A
+	 * zero-initialised rc would otherwise program 0000:0000 into the root
+	 * port, because only 0xffff means "do not write".
+	 */
+	if (rc->vendor_id == 0)
+		rc->vendor_id = 0xffff;
+	if (rc->device_id == 0)
+		rc->device_id = 0xffff;
 
 	if (!pcie->reg_base) {
 		pcie->reg_base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource_byname(pdev, "reg");
